{%- comment -%}
  The shell (海螺, owner 2026-11-18: "a minimalist conch that connects with our jewellery"). A spiral
  shell in one thin line, with a pearl at its mouth: the sea, then the jewel. The spiral draws from its
  centre outwards, the chambers and the lip follow, then the pearl rolls out of the mouth and glints.
  Decorative (aria-hidden). With reduced motion it never moves (assets/hikari.css, "The shell").
  Geometry, generated rather than drawn: r = 40·e^(0.26θ) over 2.4 turns, as smooth curves (an eighth
  of a turn each, so it stays clean drawn large), turned 135° so the mouth faces down and left; the lip
  bows out along the spiral's tangent at the mouth, and the pearl sits 17.6 units along that tangent
  (--fx/--fy: where it rolls from).
  place: 'intro' (large, on the banner as the page opens: sections/brand-hero, owner 2026-11-18 "a
  海螺 that is large and minimalist"), 'above' (small, above the heading) or 'picture' (small, white,
  in a corner of the photograph).
{%- endcomment -%}
